## PHASE 4 — Questions Feature (Student)

### T-07 · Create `src/js/features/questions-viewer.js`

This module fetches and renders question cards on the subject page.

**Key functions to implement:**

```
fetchQuestions(subjectId, db) → Array
  - Query: subject_questions WHERE subjectId == X ORDER BY order
  - Fallback: unordered query if index not ready, sort client-side
  - Filter out isActive === false

renderMcqQuestion(question, index) → HTMLElement
  - Card with question text
  - 4 option buttons (A/B/C/D)
  - On click: reveal correct/wrong with color highlight
  - Show explanation if present
  - "إجابة صحيحة ✓" / "إجابة خاطئة ✗" state

renderShortQuestion(question, index) → HTMLElement
  - Card with question text
  - "إظهار الإجابة" toggle button
  - Answer revealed on click
  - Show explanation if present

initQuestionsViewer(subjectId, db)
  - Fetch questions
  - If empty: section stays hidden (style="display:none")
  - If has content: render into #questionsList, set section display to ''
```

**No progress tracking.** Questions are stateless — every page visit starts fresh.
This avoids a login gate and keeps the feature simple.

**MCQ answer flow (locked):**
- Student clicks an option → it is immediately highlighted **correct (green)** or **wrong (red)**
- If wrong: the correct option is also highlighted green simultaneously
- All option buttons become disabled (no retry on the same question)
- Explanation text is revealed below (if present)

**Short-answer flow:**
- Student taps **"إظهار الإجابة"** toggle button
- Answer text slides/fades in below the question
- Explanation revealed below answer (if present)

**`initQuestionsViewer(subjectId, db)`**
  - Fetch questions
  - If empty: section stays hidden (`style="display:none"`)
  - If has content: render into `#questionsList`, set section `display` to `''`

