## PHASE 10 — Subject Page Tabbed Navigation

The user requested that the three main feature sections (Roadmap, Questions, Summaries) be organized into tabs rather than stacked vertically.

### T-15 · `subject.html`

**Action:** Add a tab navigation container just below the subject card (specifically, right after the `#subjectAnnouncement` section and before the feature sections).

```html
<!-- TAB NAVIGATION -->
<div class="subject-tabs-nav" id="subjectTabsNav" style="display:none;">
    <button class="subject-tab-btn" data-target="roadmapSection" id="tab-roadmap" style="display:none;">🗺️ مسار التعلم</button>
    <button class="subject-tab-btn" data-target="questionsSection" id="tab-questions" style="display:none;">❓ الأسئلة</button>
    <button class="subject-tab-btn" data-target="summariesSection" id="tab-summaries" style="display:none;">📋 الملخصات</button>
</div>
```
*Note: All tabs start hidden. They will only be revealed if their corresponding content exists.*

### T-16 · `src/css/pages/subject.css`

**Action:** Add styles for the tab bar.

```css
/* ---- Tab Navigation ---- */
.subject-tabs-nav {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin: 2rem auto 1rem;
    max-width: 760px;
    background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6);
    padding: 0.4rem;
    border-radius: 16px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.15);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
}

.subject-tab-btn {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 120px;
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
    color: #94a3b8;
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    border-radius: 12px;
    font-family: 'Cairo', sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: all 0.2s ease;
}

.subject-tab-btn:hover {
    color: #e2e8f0;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
}

.subject-tab-btn.active {
    color: #f8fafc;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--subject-accent) 40%, rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.9));
    box-shadow: 0 4px 12px color-mix(in srgb, var(--subject-accent) 20%, transparent);
}

/* Hide sections by default when tabbed */
.subject-tab-content {
    display: none;
}

.subject-tab-content.active {
    display: block;
    animation: fadeInTab 0.3s ease;
}

@keyframes fadeInTab {
    from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(5px); }
    to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
}
```

### T-17 · Feature Viewer Modifications

The feature viewers (`roadmap-viewer.js`, `questions-viewer.js`, `summaries-viewer.js`) currently reveal their own sections directly by doing `section.style.display = ''`. 

**Action:** Update all three viewers so they return a boolean (`true` if content was rendered, `false` if empty). Remove their `section.style.display = ''` logic (let the tab manager handle visibility).

### T-18 · `src/js/pages/subject-page.js`

**Action:** Implement the tab manager.

```javascript
// Wait for all viewers to load their data
const [hasRoadmap, hasQuestions, hasSummaries] = await Promise.all([
    initRoadmapViewer(subjectId, db),
    initQuestionsViewer(subjectId, db),
    initSummariesViewer(subjectId, db)
]);

// Tab Manager Logic
const tabsNav = document.getElementById('subjectTabsNav');
const tabs = {
    roadmap: { hasContent: hasRoadmap, btnId: 'tab-roadmap', sectionId: 'roadmapSection' },
    questions: { hasContent: hasQuestions, btnId: 'tab-questions', sectionId: 'questionsSection' },
    summaries: { hasContent: hasSummaries, btnId: 'tab-summaries', sectionId: 'summariesSection' }
};

let activeTabSet = false;

Object.values(tabs).forEach(tab => {
    const btn = document.getElementById(tab.btnId);
    const section = document.getElementById(tab.sectionId);
    
    // Add the tab content class for styling
    if (section) section.classList.add('subject-tab-content');

    if (tab.hasContent && btn) {
        tabsNav.style.display = 'flex'; // Show nav if at least one tab exists
        btn.style.display = ''; // Show this button
        
        // Setup click handler
        btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
            // Deactivate all
            Object.values(tabs).forEach(t => {
                document.getElementById(t.btnId)?.classList.remove('active');
                document.getElementById(t.sectionId)?.classList.remove('active');
            });
            // Activate selected
            btn.classList.add('active');
            section.classList.add('active');
        });

        // Set the first available tab as active by default
        if (!activeTabSet) {
            btn.classList.add('active');
            section.classList.add('active');
            activeTabSet = true;
        }
    }
});
```

---

## Design Decisions (Locked)

| Decision | Choice |
|---|---|
| Question progress persistence | **Stateless — resets every visit.** No localStorage, no Firestore writes. |
| MCQ wrong answer behavior | **Reveal correct immediately.** Wrong = red, correct = green, all buttons disabled. |
| Summaries video type | **Not included.** Types: `pdf`, `text`, `image` only. |
